## Demo Walkthrough

If you include a screen recording in `media/Record.mp4` (or convert it to a GIF), you can link or embed it here:

* [Watch Full App Demo Video](media/Record.mp4)

**Workflow shown in demo:**
1. Select a `.tex` source file from the workspace (`aki.tex`) and tap **Compile**.
2. Switch to the **PDFS** tab to view the generated `aki.pdf` (`166 KB`).
3. Open and preview the rendered multi-page PDF document.
4. Open the navigation drawer $\rightarrow$ **Logs** to inspect `aki_output.log` inside the bundled editor.

## Architecture & Repository Structure

This repository combines **PDF Maker** with its embedded editing components in a single unified codebase:

```text
├── app/                  # Main PDF Maker application (UI, Workspaces, Database, TeX runner)
├── xed-editor/           # Bundled Xed-Editor module (scoped to editing & saving files)
├── sora-editor/          # Sora Editor (sorax) code editor engine used by Xed-Editor
└── media/                # App screenshots and demo recordings
```

### Why Xed-Editor is Scoped

* **Single-App Experience:** Users never need to switch between external apps to edit `.tex` files or inspect `.log` outputs.
* **Database Integrity:** Xed-Editor's file management features are intentionally limited to saving modified file contents. All workspace creation, file indexing, renaming, and deletion are handled exclusively by **PDF Maker** so the local database stays synchronized with the filesystem.

